## The five tabs

The KinderCare staff app is deliberately small. Everything lives behind five tabs along the bottom:

- **Activities** — what you record about the children through the day.
- **Students** — the children in your class.
- **Calendar** — events for your class.
- **Reports** — the written reports that go to parents.
- **Notices** — announcements to parents. See [Sending Announcements](/docs/kindercare-staff-announcements).

There's no side drawer and no separate admin area to go looking for. If something isn't on one of
these five tabs, it isn't in this app.

{% callout type="note" %}
This is the teacher's app. Parents have a **separate** app with its own tabs — see
[The KinderCare Parent App](/docs/kindercare-parent-app). The two show much of the same information,
so it helps to know which one someone is describing before troubleshooting with them.
{% /callout %}

## Enrolling a child

**Students → Add Student** collects the child's details in grouped sections — personal information
(full name, student ID, date of birth), academic information (class, gender), contact information
(address, mobile number, email, parent/guardian), and additional information (nationality, religion,
RFID, allergies and medicine). You can attach a photo at the same time, taken with the **camera** or
picked from the **gallery**. Full name, student ID and class are required.

## The Students tab

The Students tab shows your class as a **grid** or a **list** — the button at the top right switches
between them. **Search by Name** narrows it down, which is usually faster than scrolling once a
class fills up. Each child also carries a badge showing whether their attendance has been marked
**today**; if the badge is missing, the attendance data may simply not have loaded, and the rest of
the app still works.

If you have no class assigned yet, the tab asks you to choose one rather than showing an empty list.

## A child's profile

Tap a child to open their profile. It is the same page parents see in their app, so the wording
matches on both sides. It has two tabs:

- **Details** — personal and contact information, the school's student ID and class, and who last
  updated the record and when. **Allergies and medicine** are shown in a highlighted red card so
  they are hard to miss.
- **Attendance** — a month-by-month calendar for the child with **Days Present**, **Working Days**
  and an **Attendance** percentage. Move between months with the calendar arrows.

Use the pencil (**Edit profile**) to change details and **Save Changes** when you are done; the
camera button changes the child's photo. Staff can edit every field apart from the **student ID**,
**class** and **Emergency Contact**, which are display-only in the app. (Parents can edit only
their phone, email, address and the photo.)

{% callout type="note" %}
If a save fails, the app shows the reason it was given rather than a generic error, so read the
message before retrying — it usually names the field that was rejected.
{% /callout %}

## The calendar

The Calendar tab is editable, not just a view: you can **add**, **edit** and **delete** events.
It loads the whole year's events, so you can page back and forward through the months without
waiting. Deleting asks for confirmation first, since parents may already have seen the event in
their app.

## Staying signed in

The app keeps you signed in across restarts, so you don't log in every morning. You only need to
sign in again after you log out.

## Account settings

**Account Settings** is intentionally minimal. Alongside your account details it offers **Request
Account Deletion** — a request to the school rather than something that happens immediately, so
submitting it does not sign you out or remove your records on the spot.

